<title>UK: Bernard Matthews buys German meat firm.</title>
<headline>Bernard Matthews buys German meat firm.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poultry meat specialist producer Bernard Matthews Plc said on Friday that it has bought the Bernhard Bartsch Group for 5.0 million stg in cash.</p>
<p>Bartsch is a specialist manufacturer of cooked meat products produced from pork and turkey based in Oldenburg, Germany.</p>
<p>It made a net profit before tax of 600,000 stg on turnover of 9.5 million for the year ended December 31.</p>
<p>&quot;Bartsch gives us a manufacturing presence in Germany which we believe will strengthen our total market position within the European Union,&quot; said Chairman Bernard Matthews.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
